      "sources": [
        "count: segment i hands off from the somite 2 h after it forms, over 2 h (D9 somites_myotomes, perSegment); the array count follows the somite count 3 h earlier: 1 at 13.33, 5 at 14.66, 10 at 17, 14 at 19, 20 at 22, 24 at 24, 29 at 26, 31 from 29 hpf; the somite record ZFA:0000155 gives the counts",
        "uStart 0.25, uEnd = 0.25 + count x 0.05 mm / axisLengthMm(t) to 0.97 (the somite array rule); lengthMm = (uEnd - uStart) x axisLengthMm / 31 so neighbours touch: 0.05 mm to 24 hpf, 0.067 at 48, 0.084 at 120, 0.183 at 720, 0.556 mm at 25 mm SL (research 03e: 59 um per myotome at 24 hpf, 700 um at 28 mm SL); uEnd 0.94 from 72 hpf so the last myomere stays inside the caudal peduncle",
        "chevronDeg 0 at formation, 20 at 22 hpf, 35 at 48, 40 from 120 hpf (BG-38; research 03a myoseptum chevronDeg 30 to 45); wFoldFraction 0.2 at 720 hpf, 1 from 2160 hpf for the adult W shape",
        "heightFraction, placement v and w (RN-01 to RN-03, phase 2 visual calibration pass): over the handoff window 13.33 to 33 hpf the template copies the somite record ZFA:0000155 height and placement at the myotome's own uMid, so a segment and its myotome occupy one volume and the trunk shows one band, not two. From 42 hpf the block fills the trunk between the spine and the skin: the dorsal edge runs 0.80 to 0.86 of the local dorsal half-height and the ventral edge 0.72 to 0.80 of the ventral half-height, the values the record already reached at 168 hpf, so the tail carries muscle to both fin-fold margins as the owner painted stage series shows at 24 and 48 hr. The medial face stays outside the notochord sheath and the width is capped at 0.88 of the skin half-width. The muscular default opacity is 0.5 (materials.ts), so the notochord and the vertebral column read through the band.",
        "lateral reach from 720 hpf (phase 3 calibration, RN-02): the lateral face reaches 0.79 to 0.82 of the skin half-width at the template station, up from 0.67 to 0.71, and the medial face does not move, so the block fills the trunk between the vertebral column and the skin. The flank stops at 0.97 of the skin half-width at every height of the block, which is what the somiteChevron section allows: its lateral face narrows to LATERAL_EDGE_FRACTION of the width at the dorsal and ventral edges while the body section narrows as an ellipse, so the 0.88 cap above needs a lateral face that follows the section."
      ]
    }
